    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a bit frustrating because i can't see anything wrong from the outside. is there anything else that could be \"hiding\" in there or causing these weird disruptions that wouldn't be obvious during a standard walkthrough? like something more unexpected?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A truly unexpected culprit could be an issue with the thermostat placement or calibration, which might be tricking the system into thinking the whole house is cool when one zone is actually overheating. Another possibility, especially in older Phoenix homes, is an issue with the insulation or the thermal envelope of that specific room, allowing heat infiltration that the AC can't overcome. Sometimes, a malfunctioning damper control motor—even if the vent looks open—is failing to open fully, effectively starving that room of cold air.",
      "source": "target",
